<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`IslandAdaptor` implements `MemeProjection` and stands as the TS shore between the composite store and the wiki's nalu engine. It carries a narrow brief, and the narrowness IS the contract:

''Inbound (projection).'' It forwards each `LarTiddlerChange` to `$tw.lares.enqueueNalu()` and stops there. Initial replay flows the same road: `emitInitialReplay()` fires one immediate change per existing tiddler, the fan-out reaches `onUriChanged`, and the next frame drains the lot inside one `wiki.transact()`.

''Outbound (TW5 edits).'' `saveTiddler` and `deleteTiddler` route through the bag-path cascade to `store.put` or `store.tombstone`, under a 400 ms capture debounce.

''Cross-bag tombstone resolution stays in TS,'' because it needs an async `getLive` on the composite.

''The echo guard belongs to the wiki.'' The adaptor asks `$tw.lares.isApplyingNalu()`; the wiki owns the apply lifetime, so one authority answers when a change is its own echo.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-the-wiki-owns>>

!! What the Nalu Engine Owns Instead

The TW5 module `nalu-engine` holds every piece the adaptor deliberately does not: the per-island buffer, the batch flush on sync (the sync gate reads as observability only), the `IslandAccumulator` wiring behind one shared queue, `flushAll(accs, budget)` for the frame drain, the `wiki.transact()` wrapping of each nalu, and the `kernel.applyDelta` calls that write the wiki.

''One writer, one place.'' Splitting the buffer across the shore and the wiki would give two owners one queue.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-cascade>>

!! The Bag-Path Cascade

`_routeBag(title)` walks `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/config/bag-paths` — newline-separated filter expressions evaluated against a single-tiddler source, first non-empty result winning. It mirrors TW5's own `$:/config/FileSystemPaths` shape, and takes the shape of `$:/config/SyncFilter` too: the shipped cascade opens with the exclusions and ends in a catch-all.

''The cascade routes; it does not decide whether to write.'' Everything a hand edits and saves travels through the CRDT and round-trips. Only a rule that NAMES what it withholds may withhold a write.

''Three outcomes, never one.'' A rule may ROUTE a title, a rule may WITHHOLD it, or no rule may reach it at all — and the third names a ROUTER GAP rather than a decision. Read as one, a gap drops the write in silence: the promise resolves, the wiki shows the edit, nothing persists, and the tiddler is gone on the next boot. The walk reports which of the three happened, and each caller acts differently on each.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/slot-of>>

!! The Last-Known-Slot Map

`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/config/slot-of` records the slot each title last landed in, this session: fed at every outbound save with the cascade's verdict, and at every inbound apply with the envelope's bag — the value the nalu stamps as `$origin-bag`.

''A delete reads it BEFORE the cascade,'' because by then the tiddler is gone and no field answers. That ordering is what lets a draft loaded from the CRDT at boot, and deleted before any save, still resolve to a slot.

The map stays volatile: one adaptor, one session.

<<~/ahu>>

